  "id": "lizardon-mega-battle",
  "name": "Lizardon Mega Battle",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "The Lizardon Mega Battle (Charizard Mega Battle) was Japan's first national championship series. Six regional cups ran from November 1997 to February 1998, from the Kobe Masara (Pallet) Cup to the Nagoya Kuchiba (Vermilion) Cup, each named after its host city and a town in the games. The top three of each junior and senior session won No. 1, No. 2 or No. 3 Trainer trophy cards in acrylic plaques, 15 of each, with an invitation to the national final at Makuhari Messe on 26 April 1998, which drew over 21,500 people. The cards reuse Mitsuhiro Arita's art of Pikachu holding a trophy from the first official tournament's trophies.\n\nThe name came back for Lizardon Mega Battle 2014, Japan's spring championship that year, which has its own entry.",
